<h2>06 · Retained failures and remaining work</h2>
<ul>{report.openReleaseGates?.map(x=><li>{x}</li>)}</ul>
<p>The original component report retains its rejected wire placement and unresolved rare-event comparisons. Later passing surface checks do not relabel those failures. The first finer induction mesh failed the 10⁻¹⁰ true-residual gate at 1.3595969434732396 × 10⁻⁵ after 16,000 iterations. RCM reordering also failed. The equilibrated solver now passes the fixed algebraic gate, but the resulting per-cell field-transfer differences are 14.0–39.7%, above the unchanged 5% mesh criterion. Four-point volume quadrature reduces these differences to 0.6–10.6%; two cells still fail. The eleven-point degree-four rule gives 0.55%, 5.28%, 10.10% and 6.12%, with three failures. These supplemental attempts do not qualify the production field.</p>
<pre>{JSON.stringify(report.retainedFailures,null,2)}</pre>
<details><summary>Supplemental source-integration diagnostics</summary><pre>{JSON.stringify({fourPoint:report.inductionQuadrature?.rows,elevenPoint:report.inductionQuadrature11?.rows,fineDirect:report.inductionDirect},null,2)}</pre></details>
<p>The 12 magnetic membrane checks compare native NEURON and two time-step halvings at 0, 10 and 100 A, including a whole-cell block. These fixtures do not fire. They check conditional membrane implementation, not a magnetic activation threshold, propagation delay or spatially converged recording.</p>
