<h2>08 · Reproduction and references</h2>
<p><code>node scripts/axon-interface/stage2/reproduce.mjs</code> runs the pinned component, native, spatial, surface, induction and cohort studies. Set <code>MRG_PYTHON</code> to the environment installed from the supplied requirements file. The script records dependency versions, source hashes, hardware and elapsed runtime. Failed numerical gates produce a failing release result; software checks cannot make the scientific release green.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Mathematical:</b> <a href="https://modeldb.science/3810">McIntyre–Richardson–Grill double cable / ModelDB 3810</a>. Motor-fiber equations assigned to a hypothetical bipolar morphology.</li>
<li><b>Experimental:</b> <a href="https://journals.plos.org/ploscompbiol/article?id=10.1371/journal.pcbi.1003220">Williams et al., 2013</a>. H134R measurements in the reported preparations and temperature-model development; no engineered ganglion calibration.</li>
<li><b>Mathematical:</b> <a href="https://modeldb.science/244414">ModelDB 244414</a>. Independent published port of the H134R equations.</li>
<li><b>Mathematical:</b> <a href="https://people.math.sc.edu/Burkardt/datasets/quadrature_rules_tet/keast4_x.txt">Keast eleven-point tetrahedral coordinates</a> and <a href="https://people.math.sc.edu/Burkardt/datasets/quadrature_rules_tet/keast4_w.txt">normalized weights</a>. Used only in supplemental source-quadrature diagnostics.</li>
<li><b>Mathematical:</b> <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29972816/">Wang, Grill and Peterchev, 2018</a>. Quasipotential treatment of conservative and nonconservative stimulation fields.</li>
<li><b>Mathematical:</b> <a href="https://www.cs.mcgill.ca/~colt2009/papers/012.pdf">Maurer and Pontil, 2009</a>. Empirical Bernstein bounds for bounded independent observations.</li>
</ul>
<p>Standing limits: measured organoid morphologies and channel fits; species/preparation calibration; heterogeneous conductivities and optical properties; electrode impedance, polarization and noise; inhibition, adaptation, plasticity and synaptic variability; validated growth-to-connectivity mapping; calibrated chronic change; and absent human evidence for proposed organoid-to-host junctions. The current B3 case avoids inventing that junction; it does not establish biological integration.</p>
